{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIzL09kZXN6YSUyMFRoZSUyMExhc3QlMjBHb29kYnllJTIwQ2luZW1hdGljJTIwRXhwZXJpZW5jZSUyMCUyODIwMjMlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Odesza The Last Goodbye Cinematic Experience","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/SKUfz2WbGYq3EptQz8krukz9UN.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/riA7k77c88EoB8UMa5ryrbA1rzk.jpg","description":"With jaw-dropping visuals and a captivating set list of fan favorites as well as unreleased remixes, see one of electronic music's biggest acts as you've never seen them before. The Last Goodbye Cinematic Experience provides a look behind-the-curtain into the process of creating ODESZA's wildly successful return to the touring stage. Since they started making music in the basement of a college house, Harrison & Clay (ODESZA) have bucked industry trends and built a creative and dedicated production team of longtime close friends. Through personal interviews with the band, their fans, and members of their creative team, the film provides an entertaining and heartfelt look at the connection between the band and their fans, how life experiences shaped the creation of their latest album, and how ODESZA grew from small-town aspiring musicians to a four-time Grammy Award-nominated, major festival headlining icon.\n\nRated G · Released 7 Jul 2023 · United States of America · Language: English · 109 min\nStudio: Seabreeze Films, Foreign Family Collective\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2023","genres":["Music","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.6","imdb_id":"tt28017875","moviedb_id":1130403,"tmdbId":1130403,"runtime":"109 min","cast":["Clayton Knight","Harrison Mills","Sean Kusanagi","Sky Iraheta","Reed Juenger","Benjamin Belleau","Kali Ridal"],"director":["Sean Kusanagi"],"released":"2023-07-07T00:00:00.000Z","country":"United States of America","language":"English","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Sean Kusanagi","character":"Director"},{"name":"Clayton K